{
  "slug": "guide/di",
  "title": "Dependency Injection in Angular",
  "description": "Learn how Angular dependency injection (DI) works: injectors, tokens, providers, hierarchical resolution, and modern inject() function.",
  "source": "https://angular.dev/guide/di",
  "status": "reviewed",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "<strong>Dependency Injection (DI)</strong> is a design pattern and architectural mechanism in which classes receive their dependencies from an external source rather than creating them directly. In Angular, DI is baked into the framework's core, making applications flexible, modular, and easy to test."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "understanding-di",
      "text": "Understanding Dependency Injection"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "In Angular, dependencies are typically services. When a component declares that it needs a service, Angular's injector automatically finds or creates the requested instance and delivers it to the component:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "file": "hero.service.ts",
      "lang": "ts",
      "code": [
        "import { Injectable } from '@angular/core';",
        "",
        "@Injectable({",
        "  providedIn: 'root', // Singleton provided application-wide",
        "})",
        "export class HeroService {",
        "  getHeroes() {",
        "    return ['Windstorm', 'Bombasto', 'Magneta'];",
        "  }",
        "}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "using-inject-function",
      "text": "Using the inject() function"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Modern Angular recommends using the <code>inject()</code> function over constructor injection for cleaner, more flexible code:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "file": "hero-list.component.ts",
      "lang": "ts",
      "code": [
        "import { Component, inject } from '@angular/core';",
        "import { HeroService } from './hero.service';",
        "",
        "@Component({",
        "  selector: 'app-hero-list',",
        "  standalone: true,",
        "  template: `",
        "    <ul>",
        "      @for (hero of heroes; track hero) {",
        "        <li>{{ hero }}</li>",
        "      }",
        "    </ul>",
        "  `",
        "})",
        "export class HeroListComponent {",
        "  private heroService = inject(HeroService);",
        "  heroes = this.heroService.getHeroes();",
        "}"
      ]
    },
